WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.709 --> 00:00:02.709
Hi guys.

00:00:02.709 --> 00:00:03.709
Dr. Berg here.

00:00:03.709 --> 00:00:08.410
In this video, we're going to talk about five
health habits for bloating and belly fat.

00:00:08.410 --> 00:00:09.679
So take note.

00:00:09.679 --> 00:00:11.480
Number one, avoid grazing.

00:00:11.480 --> 00:00:12.960
What does that mean?

00:00:12.960 --> 00:00:17.090
It means all the snacking between the meals
has to go.

00:00:17.090 --> 00:00:18.090
Why?

00:00:18.090 --> 00:00:22.589
Because every time you eat, you trigger a
hormone called insulin.

00:00:22.589 --> 00:00:25.970
Insulin creates inflammation in your colon.

00:00:25.970 --> 00:00:28.939
It just makes things swell up.

00:00:28.939 --> 00:00:34.070
What you want to do is to three meals a deal
only and if you can even two meals a day eventually,

00:00:34.070 --> 00:00:39.450
because what will happen that third meal will
be your body eating the belly fat because

00:00:39.450 --> 00:00:41.010
we want it to burn fat.

00:00:41.010 --> 00:00:42.530
Insulin is a switch.

00:00:42.530 --> 00:00:47.100
If insulin is low, you won't have any bloating
at all in your stomach.

00:00:47.100 --> 00:00:49.739
If insulin is high, you'll feel bloated.

00:00:49.739 --> 00:00:51.880
So, avoid grazing.

00:00:51.880 --> 00:00:54.409
Number two, avoid certain veggies.

00:00:54.409 --> 00:00:57.570
Now, for me, I can't eat broccoli.

00:00:57.570 --> 00:01:00.809
I like broccoli, but it bloats me.

00:01:00.809 --> 00:01:01.949
Everyone's different.

00:01:01.949 --> 00:01:04.720
You might get bloated from kale.

00:01:04.720 --> 00:01:06.460
You might get bloated from cabbage.

00:01:06.460 --> 00:01:12.360
So, whatever vegetable that bloats you, avoid
it because even though it's healthy, you don't

00:01:12.360 --> 00:01:14.770
want anything to bloat you.

00:01:14.770 --> 00:01:16.950
Number three, avoid grains and sugar.

00:01:16.950 --> 00:01:18.570
Now, this is the obvious one.

00:01:18.570 --> 00:01:20.330
You probably already know this.

00:01:20.330 --> 00:01:27.700
The gluten, the protein in grains is called
gluten, will really create inflammation in

00:01:27.700 --> 00:01:28.770
your colon.

00:01:28.770 --> 00:01:33.909
It's the number one source of IBS, irritable
bowel syndrome, diverticulitis, Crohn's and

00:01:33.909 --> 00:01:36.049
all these digestive issues.

00:01:36.049 --> 00:01:37.049
You want to avoid that.

00:01:37.049 --> 00:01:41.360
Not to mention the grains itself because grains
turn into sugar, which increases, you got

00:01:41.360 --> 00:01:42.360
it, insulin.

00:01:42.360 --> 00:01:49.009
Also, sugar, sugar creates a spike in insulin
that creates swelling of the belly, especially

00:01:49.009 --> 00:01:52.400
if you combine it with protein or even fat.

00:01:52.400 --> 00:01:57.670
So, sugar is not good at all and if you combine
it, you get a worse effect.

00:01:57.670 --> 00:02:01.960
So, avoid grains and all sugars.

00:02:01.960 --> 00:02:04.690
Number four, avoid over eating.

00:02:04.690 --> 00:02:10.270
Another obvious one, but a lot of times if
you're just in a certain mode, especially

00:02:10.270 --> 00:02:15.300
at a restaurant, you can just really down
some food, or a social event.

00:02:15.300 --> 00:02:19.610
You just keep eating and eating and eating,
or watching TV, you keep eating, eating, eating.

00:02:19.610 --> 00:02:25.660
So, I recommend that you really be conscious
about what you're eating and don't stuff yourself

00:02:25.660 --> 00:02:31.750
because it's going to take a long time to
digest that food.

00:02:31.750 --> 00:02:36.390
Number five, eating when you are not hungry.

00:02:36.390 --> 00:02:39.020
There's this whole philosophy that you have
to always eat a breakfast.

00:02:39.020 --> 00:02:41.200
I use to be the guy pushing that.

00:02:41.200 --> 00:02:45.471
Or you have to eat through the day six small
meals, even if you're not hungry because it

00:02:45.471 --> 00:02:46.680
will stimulate your metabolism.

00:02:46.680 --> 00:02:47.950
No, no, no, no.

00:02:47.950 --> 00:02:50.670
When you're not hungry, do not eat.

00:02:50.670 --> 00:02:51.670
Why?

00:02:51.670 --> 00:02:53.170
Because your body is burning fat.

00:02:53.170 --> 00:02:57.900
If you add food, the food is probably not
digested from the last meal, it's going to

00:02:57.900 --> 00:03:00.180
sit there and cause more bloating.

00:03:00.180 --> 00:03:03.250
So, only eat when you are hungry.

00:03:03.250 --> 00:03:05.420
So, I hoped this helped.

00:03:05.420 --> 00:03:07.450
Go ahead and apply this and give me some comments
below.

